\itemize{
\item A taxon that keys out at several terminal leads counts once: its steps
are the mean over its leads, as if its specimens were split evenly
among them, and its weight is not multiplied by the number of leads.
\item A couplet reached from several leads (a reticulate key) is counted by
its shortest route from the first couplet, so \code{steps} is the fewest
steps in which a result can be reached. \code{depth} is the longest route.
